# Thought Reflection (Bot1's) under Narset, Parter of Veils (Bot2's): "each opponent can't draw more than one card each turn"
# applies to each card draw (CR 121.2b), and a draw that can't happen is replaced by nothing (CR 614.17c; Narset's ruling).
# Bot1's turn 3 draw for the turn is its first card of the turn, so it can be drawn and Thought Reflection replaces it with
# two; the first of those is drawn, and the second would be the turn's second card, so it isn't drawn. Ancestral Recall's
# three draws then can't happen at all, so Thought Reflection does not replace them either: Bot1 draws one card this turn,
# where without Narset it would draw eight.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Sol Ring
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Thought Reflection
Ancestral Recall
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Black Lotus
Narset, Parter of Veils
Swamp x5
Swamp x20

